<title>FRANCE: French Treasury considering index-linked bonds.</title>
<headline>French Treasury considering index-linked bonds.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French finance ministry said on Tuesday that it was considering issuing government bonds indexed to macroeconomic variables and would sound out investors to see if there was demand for such instruments next year.</p>
<p>A finance ministry official said they were looking at the possibility of linking the bonds either to growth in gross domestic product or inflation.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
